    L1: separate edge-refusal from warrant-refusal in the attestation schema
    
    The wave-2 gate found `:refused` doing two jobs. Refusing the EDGE says the
    relation does not hold and the directive line leaves the pattern file; refusing
    the WARRANT says the evidence offered does not establish the edge, which leaves
    the directive line where it is, still only proposed. Written as one word, the
    second act could only be recorded in prose.
    
    - schema: `:warrant-refused {:by :at :note}` alongside `:state :proposed`;
      `:state :refused` keeps its meaning and its `:reason`.
    - linter: validates `:warrant-refused`; new check `:refusal-acts-distinct`
      fails a record that carries `:warrant-refused` with any state but
      `:proposed`; summary counts `:edge-refusals` and `:warrant-refusals`
      separately. `:refused-edge-removed` is unchanged, so only an edge-refusal
      still forces the directive out of the file.
    - linter: an attestation key that is not a keyword is now malformed. An
      unescaped quote in writing-coherence's row 3 `:reason` had split the string
      and left `meta-lede` as a symbol key, invisible to every schema check.
      Quote escaped; the row now reads as its author wrote it.
    - library/.spider/refusal-reclassification-2026-09-01.edn: the five existing
      `:refused` records read by hand. All five are edge-refusals by act (no
      surviving directive in any of the five source patterns); two give a
      warrant-shaped ground, recorded, not revised.
    
    The two sidecar rows that carry an ad-hoc `:refused-reason` are left for L3's
    second read, whose acceptance says to use this vocabulary.
    
    Gates: clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings; check-parens OK; test/library_graph_lint_test.clj
    6 tests / 26 assertions / 0 failures; test/spider_runner_test.clj 3 / 11 / 0.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

