**What changed** — `ccf2bf8` (+ `6031c3d` audit line-pointer, `a7c72f2` ledger). `checks/library_graph_lint.clj:301 authoring-verb-attributed-to-author?` reads the clause around the verb: it counts when the clause is impersonal (a preposition follows, no agent named — the wave-2 `Pattern authored at <path>` case), first-person, or has the record's author as subject; an active clause naming another agent does not count. An unreadable subject falls through to counting, so it refuses a warrant rather than admitting one. Counter-fixture is a real record, `emacs-7c6ac3768ecf9d2149cd9909e6224870` — joe relaying what codex-15 and `invoke-1787649777853-1018-f0693af4` had written, three `.flexiarg` paths beside the verbs. Rule version stays 3.

