Author:     Joseph Corneli <joseph.corneli@hyperreal.enterprises>
AuthorDate: Tue Sep 1 19:31:10 2026 +0000
Commit:     Joseph Corneli <joseph.corneli@hyperreal.enterprises>
CommitDate: Tue Sep 1 19:31:10 2026 +0000

    L2: reflection rule v3 -- the authoring turn is not external corroboration
    
    Wave 2 rejected one warrant by hand: a chat turn in which claude-5 announced
    the pattern file it had just written and listed that file's own references
    (system-coherence, e-7a50b862). Rule v2 could not see it -- v2 knew only who
    ran the spider (worker-seat author, Agency job envelope, spider prompt
    markers), and this record's author was none of those.
    
    v3 adds the authoring-turn class: an authoring verb within 120 characters of a
    *.flexiarg path. A turn that announces a pattern file is that pattern's author
    restating the references they just wrote, so a relation it states between that
    pattern and another comes from the authoring act, not from anyone using the
    two together. The rule is stated in the cache header beside the basis, as v2
    was, via reflection-rule.
    
    Rung 2 had no reflection check at all, which is how this record reached the
    owner's desk: rung-two-warrant? now requires at least one cited record that is
    not reflection, and the seat prompt says so.
    
    The cache filename now takes its rule version from the corpus pin rather than
    the current constant, so a record written under v2 still resolves to the index
    that classified it instead of silently rebuilding from the live store.
    Verified: system-coherence's v2 pin (basis 191738) still resolves and lints
    green.
    
    Wave-1 re-audit under v3, against the C88-pinned 56-record fixture:
    49 reflection under v2, 1 authoring turn, 49 under v3, 0 newly reflection,
    **0 changed verdicts** -- the one authoring turn in the corpus is a zai-2
    spider turn quoting the same claude-5 announcement, already reflection by its
    author. Recorded in library/aif/attestations-v3-reflection-audit.edn and
    recomputed by the test that reads it.
    
    Counter-fixture: claude-1 reviewing codex-1's NAG wiring (e-f5a7638c) says
    "flexiarg" and "authored" and names five patterns, announces no pattern file,
    and v3 leaves it alone.
    
    Gates: clj-kondo 0 errors 0 warnings (the one :info at spider-self-text?
    pre-dates this change); check-parens OK; library_graph_lint_test 7 tests /
    35 assertions; spider_runner_test 5 tests / 23 assertions; system-coherence
    section lint pass? true under its pinned cache.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

