    L3: second read of the two sidecar tag-list holds -- both warrant-refused
    
    The wave-2 spider (zai-2) proposed two edges out of
    sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts and offered one evidence record for
    both: e-8931a4eb, an f11-scribe memory record found :via :tag. claude-15
    held them for a second read on 2026-08-31 because the recorded excerpt was
    a tag list, and a tag co-occurrence may or may not state use.
    
    Read the whole record from the store rather than the excerpt. It carries
    one endpoint, not two: :evidence/subject is
    sidecar/explicit-promotion-to-facts and the body names no other pattern id.
    It is decent rung-1 evidence that the SOURCE pattern is live -- "A proposal
    is not a fact merely because its evidence body exists" restates that
    pattern's conclusion -- but an edge needs both ends, so it cannot warrant
    either target.
    
    Per edge:
    - :how -> sidecar/validation-enforcement-gate. The tag :promotion-gate
      names the promotion review that refused a deposited memory, which is the
      source pattern's own subject; the body's remedy is a query-time
      eligibility predicate, while validation-enforcement-gate.flexiarg:19 is a
      write-time check of required fields, enum constraints and store
      boundaries. Different act, same word.
    - :see-also -> sidecar/fact-lifecycle-event-types. The tag :lifecycle means
      the APM memory-proposal lifecycle inside frame 11, not the fact/warrant/
      retired event enum at fact-lifecycle-event-types.flexiarg:8,19.
    
    Both are warrant-refusals in L1's vocabulary, not edge-refusals: the
    relations are still asserted by the source file's own text (the two :cited
    strings, at explicit-promotion-to-facts.flexiarg:21 and :31), so the
    directives at :8 and :9 stay in the file, unwarranted, and each note says
    what evidence would carry it. :state stays :proposed on both.
    
    Reader is the Claude worker driven by library-build-loop.sh, recorded as
    "library-build-loop": it is not a registered Agency seat, and borrowing
    claude-13 -- named in the hold but not the reader -- would misattribute.
    
    Gates (exit codes captured to /tmp/L3gates/*.exit and tested, not read
    through a pipe): check-parens on the edited EDN exit 0 (OK); clj-kondo over
    the four gated Clojure files exit 0, 0 errors 0 warnings; bb test/
    library_graph_lint_test.clj exit 0, 7 tests / 36 assertions; bb test/
    spider_runner_test.clj exit 0, 6 tests / 33 assertions; sidecar section
    lint exit 0 before and after, pass? true, 0 failures, the sole summary
    delta :warrant-refusals 0 -> 2 with :edge-refusals 0 and the section's
    edges-by-kind unchanged at {:why 0 :how 1 :see-also 1}. The lint resolved
    the corpus-pinned cache for basis 191738, not a live crawl.
    
    No .flexiarg file changed, so this authors no @why, no post-hoc edge, and
    no similarity-inferred edge.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

