+# The one-edge price test
+
+*2026-09-01. Answers the "what this makes the next step" paragraph of
+`NOTE-the-chain-layer-exists-and-is-empty.md:105-112`: take one `@how` edge,
+write the check that says whether the method actually carries out the pattern,
+and see what it costs. Worklist item `:L4` in
+`futon3/holes/labs/library-contract/worklist.edn`. One edge. Nothing here is
+claimed for any other edge.*
+
+## The edge
+
+    peripherals/progress-heartbeat-distinct-from-cycle-completion
+      @how peripherals/canonical-typed-event-vs-side-channel
+
+Attested at `futon3/library/peripherals/attestations.edn:0`,
+`:state [:attested-by "claude-15"]`, rung 1.
+
+Chosen because it is one of nine `@how` edges in the library that are attested
+rather than proposed (`aif/` has six, `peripherals/` two, `ukrns/` one), and
+because the source pattern's own `+ evidence:` paragraph
+(`progress-heartbeat-distinct-from-cycle-completion.flexiarg:107-113`) names a
+real incident in real code — the 2026-05-24 multi-watcher fix — so there is
+somewhere to run the check *against*. Most of the other seven do not name one.
+That selection criterion is itself part of the price, and is counted below.
+
+## The check
+
+`futon3/checks/how_witness_heartbeat.clj`, run as the two snatch witnesses are:
+
+    clojure -Sdeps '{:paths ["checks"] :deps {org.clojure/core.logic {:mvn/version "1.0.1"}}}' \
+      -M -m how-witness-heartbeat
+
+It follows `how_witness_snatch.clj` exactly: a relation run forward against
+stated facts, shipped with a mirror. Facts are read at futon3c `ffb7e7bc`.
+
+Output:
+
+    witness [obligation mechanism] — obligations the METHOD carries out:
+       (none)
+    positive control (any mechanism, must be non-empty):
+       [:s1 :last-progress-at]
+       [:s3 :watchdog-silence]
+       [:s4 :last-subtask]
+    mirror (must be empty): ()
+
+    NOT ATTESTED — the method carries out 0 of 5 obligations. 3 ARE discharged
+    at this site, by state fields polled through one status map, which is the
+    side channel the method pattern names.
+
+## The price, with numbers
+
+**Wall time, 5m47s total**, split 3m12s before a line was written and 2m35s
+writing, running and registering it. The run itself — JVM start, `run*` and
+printing — takes **0.85-0.89 s** warm over three runs, 1.68 s cold.
+
+**Lines, 171 total** in the check file, of which:
+
+| part | lines |
+|---|---|
+| `ns` form and its docstring (the edge, the site, the four inventions) | 55 |
+| fact tables and their `file:line` pointers | 46 |
+| the core.logic relation, witness, positive control, mirror | 37 |
+| `-main`, printing the verdict | 30 |
+
+**Fact rows, 19**: 5 source obligations and 5 method obligations read off the
+two flexiargs, 6 site mechanisms each a `file:line` in futon3c, 3 adjudications
+saying which mechanism discharges which obligation.
+
+**Files read to produce those 19 rows, 6**:
+`progress-heartbeat-distinct-from-cycle-completion.flexiarg`,
+`canonical-typed-event-vs-side-channel.flexiarg`,
+`futon3c/src/futon3c/watcher/multi.clj`,
+`futon3c/src/futon3c/process_watchdog.clj`, `futon3c/src/futon3c/cyder.clj`,
+`futon3c/src/futon3c/transport/http.clj`.
+
+**What had to be invented — four things, none supplied by the edge**, and each
+one a place where a different choice gives a different verdict on the same
+facts:
+
+1. **Obligations.** Neither pattern marks which of its `THEN` steps is a
+   checkable obligation. Reading the five numbered steps as the obligations and
+   dropping the prose around them is a decision made in the check.
+2. **Grounding.** Nothing in the edge, in `attestations.edn:0`, or in either
+   flexiarg names a file, a function, or a system. The site came from a prose
+   evidence paragraph, which no parser reads.
+3. **A meaning for "carries out".** `README-flexiarg.md:171` says `@how` names
+   "the methods by which this pattern is carried out" and stops there. The
+   check reads it as: every source obligation is discharged at the site by a
+   mechanism that is an instance of the method. Reading it as *any one*
+   obligation, or as *the method is available*, or as *the method is
+   recommended in prose*, each flips the verdict.
+4. **The site adjudication.** Every discharge row is a human reading of a
+   source file. core.logic joins those rows; it does not produce them.
+
+## Verdict: the code is cheap, the check is expensive
+
+The 37-line relation and its 1.68-second run are cheap by any measure, and the
+mirror discipline transfers from the snatch witness unchanged. But the relation
+does not do the work that decides the verdict. The work is the 19 fact rows and
+the four inventions behind them, and those are reading and judgement — the
+snatch witness got its facts from a game's design diagrams, where a floor is a
+number and the comparison is arithmetic, and this one has to go and read source
+code and decide what counts.
+
+Concretely, on this edge: **3m12s of reading produced the 19 rows; under a
+second of core.logic consumed them.** The cost per edge here is a reading cost,
+not a compute cost, and a reading cost does not fall with more edges the way a
+compute cost would.
+
+What that means for `Q(o∣π)` is not settled here, because `Q(o∣π)` needs many
+edges and this is one. What *is* settled is that "populate and derive" prices
+the populate step wrong if it counts only the edge: an edge that is going to
+carry a derived check needs a site pointer and an obligation marking that
+nothing in `README-flexiarg.md` §5a currently asks for.
+
+## A second finding, from the same run
+
+The edge is attested and the check says NOT ATTESTED. These are answers to
+different questions and neither refutes the other. The attestation is rung 1,
+and its `:cited` field quotes the source pattern's own cross-link line — *"the
+heartbeat should be a first-class event in the transport taxonomy, not a
+parallel ping channel"* (`flexiarg:151-153`). That is a **should**. The check
+asks whether the method is applied at the site, and finds it is not: liveness
+travels as `:last-progress-at`, a key in the multi-watcher's status map
+(`multi.clj:889`, projected at `:1678`), read by the watchdog off that map
+(`process_watchdog.clj:99`), with a second liveness stamp on the CYDER process
+registry (`cyder.clj:145`) — two liveness stamps and no event type, which is
+the method pattern's own "two-channel reality" failure mode.
+
+So the edge records an aspiration, and something in the schema should say so.
+Whether that is a state, a rung, or a separate directive is not decided here.
+
+## Related
+
+- `NOTE-the-chain-layer-exists-and-is-empty.md` — the note that asked for this.
+- `futon3/checks/README.md` — the witness table, with this row added.
+- `futon3/checks/how_witness_snatch.clj` — the comparison case.

